WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.968
Episode eleven: the web UI and its AI assistant.

2
00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:18.571
This video assumes APEX installed, as in episode one, Claude Code installed and logged in, and Node.js 22.12 or later, to build the web UI once.

3
00:00:18.571 --> 00:00:22.406
First we build the web UI, in APEX's folder.

4
00:00:22.406 --> 00:00:36.148
This writes ui/dist/.

5
00:00:36.148 --> 00:00:38.816
The web UI is served by APEX's job service.

6
00:00:38.816 --> 00:00:49.729
This command starts the service in the background.

7
00:00:49.729 --> 00:00:54.034
This one prints your web-UI token, which this video hides.

8
00:00:54.034 --> 00:01:04.746
The token expires after 7 days.

9
00:01:04.746 --> 00:01:09.299
In the browser: Open http://127.0.0.1:8765/ui/.

10
00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:28.136
Sign in with the user name owner and the token from apex service token --ui --owner.

11
00:01:28.136 --> 00:01:37.918
The web UI: It shows jobs, runs, studies, predictions, optimizations, plugins and examples, and has an editor for configuration files.

12
00:01:37.918 --> 00:01:44.780
We open Examples, choose History matching, and copy the linear-Gaussian example's ES-MDA case.

13
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:55.598
The copy opens in the Editor.

14
00:01:55.598 --> 00:01:56.968
We click Validate.

15
00:01:56.968 --> 00:02:10.846
The editor shows the run's plan: members, forecasts, simulator runs.

16
00:02:10.846 --> 00:02:11.832
We click Submit.

17
00:02:11.832 --> 00:02:14.914
The job appears on the Jobs page with live events.

18
00:02:14.914 --> 00:02:18.120
Only work submitted from the web UI is listed there.

19
00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:29.074
Runs started with apex run in a terminal do not appear in the web UI.

20
00:02:29.074 --> 00:02:31.311
When it is complete, we open its run.

21
00:02:31.311 --> 00:02:46.183
The run page has a chart per metric, the steps and the run's figures.

22
00:02:46.183 --> 00:02:54.657
The assistant uses the model of [chat.llm] in service.toml, or else [agents.llm], which the other agents also use.

23
00:02:54.657 --> 00:02:57.184
Here, Claude, through Claude Code.

24
00:02:57.184 --> 00:03:06.377
Check it with claude --version.

25
00:03:06.377 --> 00:03:11.348
We put it in service.toml in the services root: here the default, in the home folder.

26
00:03:11.348 --> 00:03:22.751
The calls therefore count against your subscription's usage, not API billing.

27
00:03:22.751 --> 00:03:36.297
The service reads service.toml when it starts, so we restart it.

28
00:03:36.297 --> 00:03:38.843
We click AI Assistant in the top bar.

29
00:03:38.843 --> 00:03:44.416
The panel stays open as you move between pages, and it knows the page you are on.

30
00:03:44.416 --> 00:04:02.282
We ask which update strategies ES-MDA accepts.

31
00:04:02.282 --> 00:04:06.990
On the run we submitted, we ask whether it is healthy, and what it would change.

32
00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:28.281
The assistant uses the monitor and diagnosis agents and quotes their findings.

33
00:04:28.281 --> 00:04:35.375
Now we ask it to plan a comparison of ES-MDA with and without adaptive localization, within 20,000 simulator runs.

34
00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:58.910
When it plans a study, it writes a draft into your folder and shows a card with the draft's cost and Launch, Review in the editor and Discard.

35
00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.223
Nothing runs until you click Launch.

36
00:05:01.223 --> 00:05:05.206
The assistant itself never submits, stops or resumes anything.

37
00:05:05.206 --> 00:05:19.119
We launch it, and the study appears under Studies.

38
00:05:19.119 --> 00:05:30.018
When you are done: Stop the service with uv run apex service stop.

39
00:05:30.018 --> 00:05:35.518
Thank you for watching.
